  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 228 PM CDT Tue Sep 29 2026\n\nFriday through Tuesday:\n\nEnsembles and extended models are generally showing high\npressure moving east across the area Friday into Friday night,\nthen to the east on Saturday. This should bring a period of dry\nconditions with cooler temperatures. Lows Friday night may drop\ninto the upper 30s inland, so patchy frost may be possible \nthere.\n\nLow pressure should then shift east southeast through or north\nof the Great Lakes region Saturday night into Sunday morning,\nwith a cold front moving through the area. Moisture is lacking\nwith this feature, so it may end up being a dry frontal passage. \n\nAs a 500 mb trough develops to the northeast of the region later\nthis weekend into early next week, high pressure will move\nsoutheast through the area. This should bring more dry\nconditions, with cool temperatures lingering. Again, lows may\ndip into the upper 30s inland at times with perhaps patchy \nfrost.\n\nWood",
